+**Ending**: how a run finished, written when it happens — accepted, turned down, refused to the end, done, fallen over, stopped, or superseded. *Done* is a run with nothing to accept or turn down, which is what reading a report is. *Stopped* is a run the user replaced mid-plan with a correction or a new ask; the run that replaces it follows it in the same negotiation. *Superseded* is a plan offered and left unanswered: a new ask replaced it, and follows it in the same negotiation, or the workout it adapted was reported. A tap on it changes nothing. A run that is waiting on an answer has no ending, and neither has one that was cut.
 
