+## Amended in session 15c
+
+**A plan left unanswered is `superseded`, the seventh ending**, written when it is left behind:
+
+- a new ask opened over it; the new run follows it in the same negotiation;
+- the workout an adaptation was for is reported (the day it adapts has moved on).
+
+Not `stopped`, which is a plan nobody was shown, and not `turned down`, which is the user's answer and travels into the next brief. Before this, a new ask cleared the pending run and wrote nothing, so the reader found it *cut*.
+
 ## Consequences
 
 - **`record.Run` goes.** The model, provider and budget carried in the run's config were the identity of a run answered by one model; the model belongs to the node that did the work and goes in the record's node entries.
